{"name":"Fairy Wren","hex":"#8a6fa9","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"fairy wren","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Synonym of fairywren."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fairy_wren"}],"entries":[{"title":"Australasian wren","blocks":[{"text":"The Australasian wrens are a family, Maluridae, of small, insectivorous passerine birds endemic to Australia and New Guinea. While commonly known as wrens, they are not closely related to the true wrens. The family comprises 33 species in six genera."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/Superb_fairywren_%28Malurus_cyaneus_cyaneus%29_male_South_Bruny.jpg/330px-Superb_fairywren_%28Malurus_cyaneus_cyaneus%29_male_South_Bruny.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Australasian_wren"},{"title":"Fairy","blocks":[{"text":"A fairy is a type of mythical being or legendary creature, generally described as anthropomorphic, found in the folklore of multiple European cultures, a form of spirit, often with magical, metaphysical, supernatural, or preternatural qualities."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Falero_Luis_Ricardo_Lily_Fairy_1888.jpg/330px-Falero_Luis_Ricardo_Lily_Fairy_1888.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fairy"},{"title":"Wren","blocks":[{"text":"Wrens are a family, Troglodytidae, of small brown passerine birds. The family includes 96 species and is divided into 19 genera. All species are restricted to the New World except for the Eurasian wren that is widely distributed in the Old World. In Anglophone regions, the Eurasian wren is commonly known simply as the \"wren\", as it is the originator of the name. The name wren has been applied to other, unrelated birds, particularly the New Zealand wrens (Acanthisittidae) and the Australian wrens (Maluridae)."}],"image":"h